1
00:00:02,698 --> 00:00:04,352
[Patrick]
Just think..

2
00:00:04,439 --> 00:00:07,572
...this was once the seabed
of a prehistoric ocean.

3
00:00:07,659 --> 00:00:09,400
[Teresa]
'So?'

4
00:00:09,487 --> 00:00:11,533
So it lends perspective
in the great scheme of things

5
00:00:11,620 --> 00:00:14,362
just how insignificant,
how small, how tiny we are.

6
00:00:14,449 --> 00:00:15,754
Maybe for you.

7
00:00:15,841 --> 00:00:17,843
- Cho, what do we got?
- Tiny.

8
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:20,542
License and registration
ID him as a Ryan D'Stefano.

9
00:00:22,109 --> 00:00:23,936
Wallet was on him.
No money gone.

10
00:00:24,024 --> 00:00:26,069
Keys in the ignition.
Gas tank was empty.

11
00:00:26,156 --> 00:00:27,549
How'd he die?

12
00:00:27,636 --> 00:00:28,898
Shot from behind
at close range.

13
00:00:28,985 --> 00:00:30,247
Road rage, or paid hit?

14
00:00:30,334 --> 00:00:32,902
[indistinct chattering]

15
00:00:37,341 --> 00:00:39,604
[indistinct radio chatter]

16
00:00:41,389 --> 00:00:43,521
There's two sodas
in the drink holder.

17
00:00:43,608 --> 00:00:46,437
One's diet.
The other's regular.

18
00:00:46,524 --> 00:00:48,091
Body's on
the passenger side

19
00:00:48,178 --> 00:00:51,747
so one can assume there were
two people in the car.

20
00:00:51,834 --> 00:00:53,053
Where'd the other one go?

21
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:54,445
That's a good question.

22
00:00:54,532 --> 00:00:55,838
Anything else useful?

23
00:00:55,925 --> 00:00:57,144
No, we're still
running down the name.

24
00:00:57,231 --> 00:00:59,798
Found this in his pocket.

25
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:01,583
[sighs]
It's a start.

26
00:01:03,193 --> 00:01:04,238
[Patrick]
'Hmm.'

27
00:01:08,938 --> 00:01:10,983
[indistinct chattering]

28
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:12,724
Yeah, I know Ryan D'Stefano.

29
00:01:12,811 --> 00:01:15,553
He worked here for about,
six weeks.

30
00:01:15,640 --> 00:01:17,251
He doesn't work
for you anymore?

31
00:01:17,338 --> 00:01:18,904
Not for the last
six months.

32
00:01:18,991 --> 00:01:21,124
What kind of work was he doing
for you, Mr. Holmes?

33
00:01:21,211 --> 00:01:24,301
Security guard. I run security
here at the casino.

34
00:01:24,388 --> 00:01:26,782
Mr. D'Stefano
is a convicted criminal.

35
00:01:26,869 --> 00:01:29,132
He's served time
for burglary and armed robbery.

36
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:31,526
You hire ex-cons to work
for security for you often?

37
00:01:31,613 --> 00:01:33,702
No, I don't,
and that's why I fired him.

38
00:01:33,789 --> 00:01:35,747
How'd he get past
the background check?

39
00:01:35,834 --> 00:01:39,055
[Mr. Holmes]
'Look, I can't access
police records as fast as you.'

40
00:01:39,142 --> 00:01:41,275
Once I found out,
I dealt with it.

41
00:01:41,362 --> 00:01:44,147
Yes, you seem like a man
that deals with things.

42
00:01:44,234 --> 00:01:46,236
You got that right.

43
00:01:46,323 --> 00:01:48,369
Did Mr. D'Stefano
form any relationships

44
00:01:48,456 --> 00:01:51,198
while he was working here?
Friends or enemies?

45
00:01:51,285 --> 00:01:52,460
[Mr. Holmes]
'No, he kept pretty much
to himself.'

46
00:01:52,547 --> 00:01:53,939
Can you think of anybody

47
00:01:54,026 --> 00:01:56,377
who may have wanted
to harm Mr. D'Stefano?

48
00:01:56,464 --> 00:01:57,987
No.

49
00:01:58,074 --> 00:02:00,207
We need to talk to your boss.
Where is he?

50
00:02:00,294 --> 00:02:02,687
That would be Mr. Shaw.
He's not here today.

51
00:02:02,774 --> 00:02:04,689
What about any kind of paperwork
you might have on D'Stefano?

52
00:02:04,776 --> 00:02:05,908
Where's that?

53
00:02:05,995 --> 00:02:07,127
This way.

54
00:02:08,215 --> 00:02:09,912
Where's the other guy?

55
00:02:09,999 --> 00:02:13,655
Ah. He does that.
He'll be back later.

56
00:02:13,742 --> 00:02:16,092
This way.

57
00:02:16,179 --> 00:02:18,877
The handcuffs are no longer
on me. They are on you.

58
00:02:18,964 --> 00:02:21,053
[lounge music]

59
00:02:25,145 --> 00:02:28,017
And here's your watch,
good as new.

60
00:02:28,104 --> 00:02:30,062
A round of applause
for our volunteer.

61
00:02:38,288 --> 00:02:40,464
In the lamaseries
of the orient--

62
00:02:40,551 --> 00:02:43,250
Hey, Jack,
where's my 50 bucks?

63
00:02:43,337 --> 00:02:46,296
[indistinct chattering]

64
00:02:46,383 --> 00:02:49,125
From the lamaseries
of the orient..

65
00:02:49,212 --> 00:02:52,998
...to the ancient texts
of Atlantis..

66
00:02:53,085 --> 00:02:56,611
...I have found the key to
controlling the dark energies..

67
00:02:56,698 --> 00:02:57,960
...of the universe.

68
00:02:59,135 --> 00:03:01,703
[instrumental music]

69
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:02,834
[cape whooshes]

70
00:03:02,921 --> 00:03:05,924
Channeling these energies..

71
00:03:06,011 --> 00:03:08,144
...I would transport
my beautiful assistant

72
00:03:08,231 --> 00:03:09,711
across the stage..

73
00:03:11,582 --> 00:03:13,976
...to reappear in this box.

74
00:03:14,063 --> 00:03:15,760
Seriously, Jack.
I just want what's mine.

75
00:03:15,847 --> 00:03:19,242
'Where's my 50 bucks?'

76
00:03:19,329 --> 00:03:20,591
'50 bucks.'

77
00:03:25,814 --> 00:03:27,511
'Jack, come on.'

78
00:03:27,598 --> 00:03:30,558
Lowlife piker!
I want my scratch!

79
00:03:30,645 --> 00:03:32,473
[Patrick laughing]

80
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:33,561
Damn it!

81
00:03:36,128 --> 00:03:38,392
Hey, Jack, calm down.
Don't recognize me?

82
00:03:38,479 --> 00:03:41,264
Patrick Jane?
I should have known.

83
00:03:41,351 --> 00:03:43,397
Little heckling,
and you blow a simple pass.

84
00:03:43,484 --> 00:03:45,529
You're losing
your touch, Jack.

85
00:03:45,616 --> 00:03:47,096
Oh!

86
00:03:47,183 --> 00:03:48,358
You ruined my act.

87
00:03:49,316 --> 00:03:50,752
It was good to see you.

88
00:03:53,276 --> 00:03:54,973
[sniffles]

89
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:57,541
[theme music]

90
00:04:05,636 --> 00:04:07,159
Yeah, I'm doing pretty good
here all around.

91
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,074
This job's just
temporary, really

92
00:04:09,161 --> 00:04:11,338
until the new floor show
at Caesars.

93
00:04:11,425 --> 00:04:13,905
That's next, probably.

94
00:04:13,992 --> 00:04:15,733
Oh, that's great.

95
00:04:15,820 --> 00:04:18,214
Yeah. I'm excited.
I am super excited.

96
00:04:21,739 --> 00:04:23,045
What happened, Jack?

97
00:04:24,525 --> 00:04:26,135
You were headed
for the top.

98
00:04:26,222 --> 00:04:27,397
I still am.

99
00:04:29,486 --> 00:04:31,271
I still am,
I still am.

100
00:04:31,358 --> 00:04:33,316
[scoffs]

101
00:04:33,403 --> 00:04:34,622
I just, uh..

102
00:04:37,189 --> 00:04:40,192
...I got sidetracked.
I got caught up in some stuff.

103
00:04:45,459 --> 00:04:47,896
I got busted for drugs.
I did some time.

104
00:04:47,983 --> 00:04:50,507
It's not a big deal.
Just, uh..

105
00:04:50,594 --> 00:04:54,032
...just messed with
my bookings a little, so..

106
00:04:54,119 --> 00:04:56,731
That's showbiz. Right?

107
00:04:56,818 --> 00:04:59,864
But I'm working my way
back up, so..

108
00:04:59,951 --> 00:05:02,476
Blah blah blah, that's me.
What you been up to, Patrick?

109
00:05:06,262 --> 00:05:07,655
I work with the police.

110
00:05:09,613 --> 00:05:11,093
CBI.

111
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:13,225
I'm investigating a murder.

112
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:16,141
- You're kidding me.
- No. No.

113
00:05:16,228 --> 00:05:17,229
In fact, uh..

114
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:19,014
[clears throat]

115
00:05:19,101 --> 00:05:21,277
This is my bit. Uh..

116
00:05:21,364 --> 00:05:22,626
...do you
recognize this man?

117
00:05:25,194 --> 00:05:27,196
No, never seen him.

118
00:05:27,283 --> 00:05:28,284
Seriously.

119
00:05:30,504 --> 00:05:31,853
N--y--no, no.

120
00:05:33,898 --> 00:05:37,032
How are you, of all people,
working with the cops?

121
00:05:37,119 --> 00:05:38,860
You didn't hear
what happened?

122
00:05:38,947 --> 00:05:40,818
No. Hear what?

123
00:05:40,905 --> 00:05:42,167
[whispers]
Eh, it's a long story.

124
00:05:44,822 --> 00:05:45,867
I'm here.

125
00:05:48,173 --> 00:05:50,828
Well, I'm sorry I can't be
of more assistance, officer.

126
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:54,832
Good to see you
so well, Jack.

127
00:05:54,919 --> 00:05:56,660
Yeah, yeah.

128
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:58,967
Last time I saw you
was 16 years ago

129
00:05:59,054 --> 00:06:01,143
when you opened for me
in Kansas City

130
00:06:01,230 --> 00:06:04,625
and for what it's worth,
you don't look a day older.

131
00:06:04,712 --> 00:06:07,062
Well, thank you,
but you're mistaken, Patrick.

132
00:06:07,149 --> 00:06:08,759
It's you who opened for me.

133
00:06:08,846 --> 00:06:11,719
- Your memory's going.
- Mm. Mentalists.

134
00:06:13,111 --> 00:06:16,114
Big talkers.No skills.

135
00:06:16,201 --> 00:06:18,639
[chuckles]

136
00:06:18,726 --> 00:06:19,901
See you.

137
00:06:24,645 --> 00:06:26,734
Ballistics reports
the slugs came from a .38.

138
00:06:26,821 --> 00:06:28,518
Explains why there were no shell
casings at the crime scene.

139
00:06:28,605 --> 00:06:29,911
We got D'Stefano's prints
all over the car

140
00:06:29,998 --> 00:06:31,216
and on one
of the soda cups.

141
00:06:31,303 --> 00:06:32,957
There's different prints
on the other cup.

142
00:06:33,044 --> 00:06:34,568
Haven't come up with anything
yet, but we're still searching.

143
00:06:34,655 --> 00:06:36,004
If they're in the system,
we'll find 'em.

144
00:06:36,091 --> 00:06:38,006
Okay, what have we learned
about D'Stefano?

145
00:06:38,093 --> 00:06:39,921
Grew up near
the Oregon border.

146
00:06:40,008 --> 00:06:42,184
Brother claimed D'Stefano was
getting his life back on track

147
00:06:42,271 --> 00:06:43,490
since he was released
on parole.

148
00:06:43,577 --> 00:06:45,317
They always say that,
don't they?

149
00:06:45,405 --> 00:06:48,103
All tracks, though,
new town, new job, fresh start

150
00:06:48,190 --> 00:06:49,713
leave all
the bad influences behind.

151
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,324
Getting fired would have
put a dent in that.

152
00:06:52,412 --> 00:06:53,717
What'd he do
after he lost his job?

153
00:06:53,804 --> 00:06:55,632
- Nothing.
- What do you mean, "nothing"?

154
00:06:55,719 --> 00:06:57,808
He didn't get another job?
He didn't go back up north?

155
00:06:57,895 --> 00:07:00,289
Nope, he just hung around in
San Refugio until he was killed.

156
00:07:00,376 --> 00:07:02,639
Here's something.
I called his parole officer.

157
00:07:02,726 --> 00:07:04,424
He said D'Stefano
got into a scuffle

158
00:07:04,511 --> 00:07:07,296
with an unknown individual
at a bar outside San Refugio.

159
00:07:07,383 --> 00:07:08,558
PO gave him a break
and let it slide.

160
00:07:08,645 --> 00:07:09,994
When was that?

161
00:07:10,081 --> 00:07:11,735
Couple months ago,
after he got fired.

162
00:07:11,822 --> 00:07:13,345
Okay, what about the casino?
We finding any connection?

163
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,173
Yeah, owner's a guy
named Nicky Shaw.

164
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,088
He's reputed to be mobbed up,
for what it's worth.

165
00:07:17,175 --> 00:07:19,613
Cho, you and Rigsby
look into D'Stefano's movements

166
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:22,442
leading up to his murder.
See if you can find anything.

167
00:07:22,529 --> 00:07:24,052
Grace, follow up
on the bar fight.

168
00:07:24,139 --> 00:07:25,445
Will do, boss.

169
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:30,754
Are you planning on taking
any interest in this case?

170
00:07:30,841 --> 00:07:32,103
I'm looking for clues.

171
00:07:34,932 --> 00:07:36,717
Yes, in the newspaper.

172
00:07:36,804 --> 00:07:38,980
Besides, I heard
every single word.

173
00:07:39,067 --> 00:07:41,417
- Really?
- Yes.

174
00:07:41,504 --> 00:07:43,288
Our victim is either
a hardened criminal

175
00:07:43,375 --> 00:07:46,161
or a tragically misunderstood
Dickensian waif.

176
00:07:46,248 --> 00:07:49,120
Also, the casino may be
connected to the mafia.

177
00:07:49,207 --> 00:07:50,731
Okay, so what
do you think?

178
00:07:52,994 --> 00:07:54,386
"What do I think?"

179
00:07:55,300 --> 00:07:56,606
I think I'm hungry.

180
00:07:58,216 --> 00:08:00,654
[instrumental music]

181
00:08:04,745 --> 00:08:07,182
[country music]

182
00:08:11,142 --> 00:08:13,144
Howdy.

183
00:08:13,231 --> 00:08:14,668
What can I do you for?

184
00:08:14,755 --> 00:08:16,321
I'm curious about a fight
that happened here

185
00:08:16,408 --> 00:08:18,149
a couple months ago,
involving this guy.

186
00:08:20,021 --> 00:08:23,677
That's Ryan. Yeah. They went
at each other pretty good.

187
00:08:24,678 --> 00:08:26,549
You knew Mr. D'Stefano?

188
00:08:26,636 --> 00:08:28,246
What's this about?

189
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:31,380
He was murdered. You don't
know anything about that?

190
00:08:31,467 --> 00:08:33,687
What happened?

191
00:08:33,774 --> 00:08:35,471
He was shot.

192
00:08:35,558 --> 00:08:36,777
What can you tell me
about him?

193
00:08:36,864 --> 00:08:39,344
You know,
he was a good guy, just..

194
00:08:39,431 --> 00:08:41,042
...hotheaded.

195
00:08:41,129 --> 00:08:43,087
Is that how
the fight started?

196
00:08:43,174 --> 00:08:45,960
Yeah, I mean, after he lost
his job at the casino

197
00:08:46,047 --> 00:08:48,397
he was always going on and on
about getting back at them

198
00:08:48,484 --> 00:08:52,096
so, you know, when the guy
who fired him showed up one day

199
00:08:52,183 --> 00:08:53,576
yeah, Ryan lost it.

200
00:08:53,663 --> 00:08:54,882
Was that Shaw,
the casino owner?

201
00:08:54,969 --> 00:08:56,492
Or the other guy,
head of security?

202
00:08:56,579 --> 00:08:59,800
I don't know. Big black guy
with a shaved head.

203
00:09:02,019 --> 00:09:04,718
Finished eating?
D'Stefano got in a bar fight

204
00:09:04,805 --> 00:09:07,503
with the security guy
from the casino, Dante Holmes.

205
00:09:07,590 --> 00:09:09,244
[Teresa on phone]
'I think we should
talk to him again.'

206
00:09:09,331 --> 00:09:11,725
Oh, interesting.
I'll take care of it.

207
00:09:11,812 --> 00:09:14,249
W-what do you mean?
Where are you?

208
00:09:14,336 --> 00:09:16,991
Uh, be back soon.
We'll talk then.

209
00:09:17,078 --> 00:09:19,210
Sorry about that, Mr. Shaw.

210
00:09:19,297 --> 00:09:21,517
So rumor has it
that you're a made man.

211
00:09:23,127 --> 00:09:26,653
Did you have D'Stefano whacked,
rubbed out, smudged

212
00:09:26,740 --> 00:09:28,698
whatever it is
the phrase you use?

213
00:09:28,785 --> 00:09:30,961
That's funny.

214
00:09:31,048 --> 00:09:34,008
Look, is it an embarrassment
that we hired a convicted felon?

215
00:09:34,095 --> 00:09:36,837
Of course. Does that
implicate us in his death?

216
00:09:36,924 --> 00:09:38,621
Not at all.

217
00:09:38,708 --> 00:09:41,363
Does that make us liable
in any way? I don't think so.

218
00:09:44,148 --> 00:09:45,976
What about the fight
that you had with D'Stefano?

219
00:09:47,325 --> 00:09:48,544
What fight?

220
00:09:52,548 --> 00:09:56,030
He was drunk and angry at me
for canning him.

221
00:09:56,117 --> 00:09:58,249
Can't blame him for that.

222
00:09:58,336 --> 00:09:59,947
So I tuned him up a little.

223
00:10:00,034 --> 00:10:01,513
Saw no reason
to speak about it

224
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:04,255
seeing as there was no
connection to him getting shot.

225
00:10:04,342 --> 00:10:06,214
Well, that seems
reasonable enough

226
00:10:06,301 --> 00:10:07,694
and who wants
that kind of publicity?

227
00:10:08,869 --> 00:10:09,913
Right.

228
00:10:11,828 --> 00:10:13,438
Look, I run
a nice establishment here.

229
00:10:13,525 --> 00:10:16,833
'Everything is the best.
Next month, I've got'

230
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:19,270
'an international
poker tournament coming in.'

231
00:10:19,357 --> 00:10:22,186
Top cable coverage.
It's gonna be big.

232
00:10:22,273 --> 00:10:24,188
You didn't know
about the fight?

233
00:10:24,275 --> 00:10:26,408
No.

234
00:10:26,495 --> 00:10:28,149
And you don't mind
that Holmes here

235
00:10:28,236 --> 00:10:31,195
was withholding
that information from you?

236
00:10:31,282 --> 00:10:33,023
- No.
- Hmm.

237
00:10:33,110 --> 00:10:35,112
Look, is there anything else
you'd like to know?

238
00:10:35,199 --> 00:10:37,245
My business is an open book
to law enforcement.

239
00:10:37,332 --> 00:10:39,029
Mm. Mm.

240
00:10:39,116 --> 00:10:40,988
[lounge music]

241
00:10:42,685 --> 00:10:45,601
[applause]

242
00:10:46,646 --> 00:10:47,951
No, I'm fine, thanks.

243
00:10:52,477 --> 00:10:54,871
[instrumental music]

244
00:10:56,743 --> 00:10:57,831
Enjoy the show.

245
00:11:00,355 --> 00:11:03,010
[music continues]

246
00:11:06,753 --> 00:11:08,493
What's up?

247
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,582
We found the gas station where
D'Stefano and his passenger

248
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:12,802
got gas and sodas.
We got an ID on the passenger.

249
00:11:12,889 --> 00:11:14,195
[Cho]
'Her name's Holly Danvers.'

250
00:11:14,282 --> 00:11:15,413
Paid for the drinks
using a credit card.

251
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,067
Hasn't used it since.

252
00:11:17,154 --> 00:11:19,287
Couple of drug priors.
There's an address there.

253
00:11:19,374 --> 00:11:22,029
Nice work.
Go and get her, but be careful.

254
00:11:22,116 --> 00:11:23,857
If she executed D'Stefano
in cold blood

255
00:11:23,944 --> 00:11:25,119
she's likely
to put up a fight.

256
00:11:25,206 --> 00:11:26,686
Alright. We'll call in,
we get anything.

257
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:31,603
[instrumental music]

258
00:11:34,128 --> 00:11:35,564
[engine turns off]

259
00:11:38,741 --> 00:11:41,613
[dog barking]

260
00:11:41,701 --> 00:11:44,007
Can I, uh, help you gents?

261
00:11:44,094 --> 00:11:45,879
[Wayne]
CBI.

262
00:11:45,966 --> 00:11:48,577
[Cho]
Do you know a woman
named Holly Danvers?

263
00:11:48,664 --> 00:11:51,536
Sure. We know Holly.

264
00:11:51,623 --> 00:11:53,887
Trailer 60. Fine tenant.

265
00:11:53,974 --> 00:11:57,629
Huh. Her roommate Cheryl's
a pushy one, though.

266
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,544
Complains about
the water pressure.

267
00:11:59,631 --> 00:12:01,546
Is she in her trailer?

268
00:12:01,633 --> 00:12:04,375
No, she went away with a young
fella couple of days ago.

269
00:12:05,507 --> 00:12:07,901
My wife sees everything.

270
00:12:07,988 --> 00:12:09,685
Nobody gets away
with anything around here.

271
00:12:10,991 --> 00:12:12,166
You recognize this man?

272
00:12:13,428 --> 00:12:15,038
Yeah, that's him.

273
00:12:15,125 --> 00:12:17,911
Yeah, I remember because
one of 'em forgot something

274
00:12:17,998 --> 00:12:19,434
and then he went
back to get it.

275
00:12:19,521 --> 00:12:20,827
Can we talk to the roommate?

276
00:12:20,914 --> 00:12:23,873
- I don't think she's in.
- Oh.

277
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,832
I stopped by earlier
to check her propane

278
00:12:25,919 --> 00:12:27,485
but, uh,
she didn't answer.

279
00:12:27,572 --> 00:12:29,183
Any chance we could take
a look around the trailer?

280
00:12:29,270 --> 00:12:30,750
Be a big help to us.

281
00:12:30,837 --> 00:12:33,013
Oh, of course you can.
We run an honest place.

282
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:35,624
- Go get the keys.
- Yes, ma'am.

283
00:12:35,711 --> 00:12:38,322
Head over.
He'll come meet you.

284
00:12:38,409 --> 00:12:39,584
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

285
00:12:42,544 --> 00:12:45,242
[birds chirping]

286
00:12:50,334 --> 00:12:52,946
CBI. We need
to speak to you.

287
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:54,034
See? Nobody home.

288
00:12:55,470 --> 00:12:56,906
Can you unlock it
for me, please?

289
00:12:56,993 --> 00:12:59,213
Yeah, sure.

290
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,041
[keys jangle]

291
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:03,695
Stand back.

292
00:13:05,436 --> 00:13:06,916
[door creaks]

293
00:13:08,178 --> 00:13:09,963
Hello?

294
00:13:10,050 --> 00:13:12,922
[fan squeaking]

295
00:13:14,706 --> 00:13:16,099
Your park manager
let us in.

296
00:13:17,971 --> 00:13:20,277
[intense music]

297
00:13:26,283 --> 00:13:28,895
Cheryl? Cheryl?

298
00:13:29,809 --> 00:13:31,158
'Oh, damn it!'

299
00:13:39,166 --> 00:13:40,515
[Jack]
'Prepare yourselves,
ladies and gentlemen'

300
00:13:40,602 --> 00:13:44,084
to be terrified and amazed.

301
00:13:44,171 --> 00:13:46,956
[Survivor's "Eye Of The Tiger"
playing]

302
00:13:47,043 --> 00:13:49,741
Hey. What did you do to me?
I can't feel my toes.

303
00:13:50,612 --> 00:13:53,136
[Patrick laughing]

304
00:13:54,442 --> 00:13:55,530
Where are my toes?

305
00:13:56,748 --> 00:13:57,880
'I can't feel my toes.'

306
00:13:59,273 --> 00:14:00,709
Hey. Hey, hey,
look, look, look.

307
00:14:00,796 --> 00:14:02,624
Her head's in a box,
but she's still talking.

308
00:14:03,494 --> 00:14:04,669
[clapping]

309
00:14:04,756 --> 00:14:05,888
That is crazy.

310
00:14:07,281 --> 00:14:08,325
Crazy.

311
00:14:09,805 --> 00:14:11,720
Holly Danvers is
our number one suspect.

312
00:14:11,807 --> 00:14:13,113
What do we know about her?

313
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,723
Well, according
to her parole records

314
00:14:14,810 --> 00:14:16,290
Holly Danvers did everything
she was supposed to.

315
00:14:16,377 --> 00:14:18,031
She got clean and stayed clean.

316
00:14:18,118 --> 00:14:20,860
Passed all her drug tests,
went to regular counseling

317
00:14:20,947 --> 00:14:22,383
even got a good job
as a waitress

318
00:14:22,470 --> 00:14:23,645
at a place
called Big Frank's.

319
00:14:23,732 --> 00:14:24,951
Big Frank's
outside San Refugio?

320
00:14:25,038 --> 00:14:26,604
Yeah.

321
00:14:26,691 --> 00:14:27,649
That's where D'Stefano
got into his fight.

322
00:14:27,736 --> 00:14:28,911
'They must have met there.'

323
00:14:28,998 --> 00:14:30,565
Love triangle
gone wrong, maybe?

324
00:14:30,652 --> 00:14:32,872
D'stefano and Danvers
hook up, then she catches him

325
00:14:32,959 --> 00:14:34,525
cheating on her with
the roommate kills 'em both.

326
00:14:34,612 --> 00:14:36,223
Does she have
a history of violence?

327
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:38,921
- No.
- We need to dig deeper.

328
00:14:39,008 --> 00:14:41,141
Van Pelt, go to Big Frank's.
See what you can learn.

329
00:14:41,228 --> 00:14:42,185
Alright.

330
00:14:43,795 --> 00:14:45,275
[sighs]

331
00:14:45,362 --> 00:14:46,624
[bartender]
'Order up!'

332
00:14:46,711 --> 00:14:49,366
Holly? She's one of
my best waitresses. Why?

333
00:14:49,453 --> 00:14:51,455
When was the last time
you spoke with her?

334
00:14:51,542 --> 00:14:53,240
She was supposed
to be working today.

335
00:14:53,327 --> 00:14:55,590
She called in this morning, said
she had to miss a couple shifts.

336
00:14:55,677 --> 00:14:56,939
Order up!

337
00:14:57,026 --> 00:14:58,506
She called in?
What'd she say?

338
00:15:00,508 --> 00:15:03,032
Needed time off
for a personal matter.

339
00:15:03,119 --> 00:15:05,817
Seemed kind of cranky,
so I didn't push.

340
00:15:05,905 --> 00:15:09,430
Like I said,
she's one of my best. Hey!

341
00:15:09,517 --> 00:15:11,388
Hello. Order up.

342
00:15:13,042 --> 00:15:14,304
Thank you.

343
00:15:16,132 --> 00:15:17,090
[Jack]
'I don't know.'

344
00:15:17,177 --> 00:15:19,135
[knock on door]

345
00:15:22,182 --> 00:15:23,748
Hey, Patrick.
What is it?

346
00:15:23,835 --> 00:15:26,360
Well, I caught the show.
It was great. Very smooth.

347
00:15:26,447 --> 00:15:29,537
Uh, the sphinx, nicely played.
Love the Blammo box.

348
00:15:29,624 --> 00:15:32,192
Of course it's all about
the assistant. Patrick.

349
00:15:32,279 --> 00:15:34,150
- Oh, I'm Trish.
- We're old friends.

350
00:15:34,237 --> 00:15:35,325
[whispers]
Oh.

351
00:15:38,415 --> 00:15:40,548
[Jack]
'Yeah.'

352
00:15:40,635 --> 00:15:42,680
Sorry. Uh,
this is Vincent and Skiddy.

353
00:15:42,767 --> 00:15:44,552
They're young magicians
I am mentoring.

354
00:15:46,728 --> 00:15:48,556
[whispers]
Hi.

355
00:15:48,643 --> 00:15:50,732
Jack and I used to work
the carnival circuit together.

356
00:15:50,819 --> 00:15:52,952
Mentoring, huh?
Well, that's great.

357
00:15:53,039 --> 00:15:55,476
Used to be this guy was so tight
he wouldn't tell you the time.

358
00:15:55,563 --> 00:15:57,869
Uh, still owes me 50 bucks
from what, 16 years ago?

359
00:15:57,957 --> 00:15:59,306
I don't remember
this 50 bucks.

360
00:15:59,393 --> 00:16:01,047
Of course you don't.
You know what?

361
00:16:01,134 --> 00:16:03,832
I'm gonna let that slide.
Anyway, I have to run.

362
00:16:03,919 --> 00:16:07,314
Um, it was a great act.
Nice to meet you.

363
00:16:07,401 --> 00:16:08,924
- Be good.
- 'Thanks.'

364
00:16:09,011 --> 00:16:11,971
Hey, uh, I'll call you.
We'll, we'll get together, okay?

365
00:16:12,058 --> 00:16:13,494
- Sure, Jack.
- Alright.

366
00:16:18,586 --> 00:16:21,458
[indistinct chattering]

367
00:16:25,593 --> 00:16:27,943
[intense music]

368
00:16:40,695 --> 00:16:42,001
[door opens]

369
00:16:43,350 --> 00:16:45,221
[cellphone ringing]

370
00:16:45,308 --> 00:16:46,657
Hello, Lisbon.

371
00:16:46,744 --> 00:16:48,442
'You wondering
when I'm coming back?'

372
00:16:48,529 --> 00:16:50,748
No. Not at all.
I wouldn't want to impose.

373
00:16:50,835 --> 00:16:53,403
Whenever you find the time
is okay with me.

374
00:16:53,490 --> 00:16:55,579
Ah. Sarcasm.
Doesn't suit you much at all.

375
00:16:59,148 --> 00:17:02,499
I'm working the case.
In fact, I've almost cracked it.

376
00:17:02,586 --> 00:17:04,153
Really? So have we.

377
00:17:05,372 --> 00:17:07,722
Really? What do you got?

378
00:17:07,809 --> 00:17:09,637
[Teresa on phone]
'It looks to be
a crime of passion.'

379
00:17:09,724 --> 00:17:11,726
'A woman named Holly Danvers
was the last person'

380
00:17:11,813 --> 00:17:13,684
'to see D'Stefano
before his death'

381
00:17:13,771 --> 00:17:16,122
and we found her roommate
dead in their trailer.

382
00:17:16,209 --> 00:17:17,993
Ahh.

383
00:17:18,080 --> 00:17:20,126
[Teresa on phone]
'Yeah, and Danvers
was a waitress'

384
00:17:20,213 --> 00:17:21,997
'at the bar D'Stefano
got in a fight at.'

385
00:17:22,084 --> 00:17:24,608
Ooh. Well, now it seems
to make sense.

386
00:17:24,695 --> 00:17:26,393
Yeah, because I just
explained it to you.

387
00:17:26,480 --> 00:17:27,742
When are you coming back?

388
00:17:28,656 --> 00:17:31,572
[intense music]

389
00:17:31,659 --> 00:17:33,530
We'll talk later, Lisbon.
Thanks.

390
00:17:34,923 --> 00:17:36,403
[Teresa on phone]
'Wait. Jane..'

391
00:17:37,969 --> 00:17:40,320
[intense music]

392
00:17:41,321 --> 00:17:42,626
Security's too tight.

393
00:17:42,713 --> 00:17:45,238
It was 12 minutes, man.
We checked it twice.

394
00:17:45,325 --> 00:17:47,109
Sorry, man.

395
00:17:47,196 --> 00:17:49,720
Gosh, guys.
There's gotta..

396
00:17:49,807 --> 00:17:51,070
There's no way.

397
00:17:54,073 --> 00:17:55,378
We tried, man.

398
00:17:56,684 --> 00:17:59,382
[intense music]

399
00:18:01,167 --> 00:18:02,646
[engine starts]

400
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,345
[tires screeching]

401
00:18:06,259 --> 00:18:08,130
Thanks. Thank you.

402
00:18:09,566 --> 00:18:11,090
[grunts]

403
00:18:12,308 --> 00:18:14,615
Hello, Jack.

404
00:18:14,702 --> 00:18:16,443
[exhales deeply]
Where'd you come from?

405
00:18:19,707 --> 00:18:21,926
I know what's going on.

406
00:18:22,013 --> 00:18:25,147
What are you talking about?
You, you been following me?

407
00:18:25,234 --> 00:18:27,802
The way you fell apart
onstage when I yelled

408
00:18:27,889 --> 00:18:29,151
was the first clue.

409
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,112
Then you lied about
knowing D'Stefano

410
00:18:33,199 --> 00:18:37,333
and now you're palling around
with a couple of ex-cons.

411
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:39,292
Your friends are more
professional than they look.

412
00:18:39,379 --> 00:18:41,903
I must say that. They did
a good job of casing this place.

413
00:18:41,990 --> 00:18:43,252
What do you mean?
What place?

414
00:18:43,339 --> 00:18:45,515
You're planning
to rob the casino, Jack.

415
00:18:45,602 --> 00:18:47,778
- There's no point in hiding it.
- Shut up.

416
00:18:47,865 --> 00:18:49,084
You can get me
in a lot of trouble

417
00:18:49,171 --> 00:18:50,520
people hear you
talking like that.

418
00:18:50,607 --> 00:18:51,652
Question is, why?

419
00:18:51,739 --> 00:18:54,524
You're not
the casino-robbing type.

420
00:18:54,611 --> 00:18:56,657
I don't know
what you're talking about

421
00:18:56,744 --> 00:18:58,746
and you should
leave it alone.

422
00:18:58,833 --> 00:19:00,704
You're scared.
I knew that from the first

423
00:19:00,791 --> 00:19:03,142
but not for yourself,
for someone you care about.

424
00:19:03,229 --> 00:19:05,666
Cut it out. I mean it.
Walk away.

425
00:19:05,753 --> 00:19:07,320
Holly Danvers
is your girlfriend.

426
00:19:07,407 --> 00:19:08,799
She's been kidnapped

427
00:19:08,886 --> 00:19:11,280
by whoever's making you
rob the casino.

428
00:19:12,629 --> 00:19:13,848
Yes.

429
00:19:16,329 --> 00:19:18,722
But it can't be robbed.
It's impossible.

430
00:19:18,809 --> 00:19:20,681
Really?

431
00:19:20,768 --> 00:19:22,161
I mean,
it's not Fort Knox.

432
00:19:23,553 --> 00:19:24,946
Is it really that hard?

433
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:26,643
I've been looking at it
every which way.

434
00:19:26,730 --> 00:19:28,428
I can't see
how it can be done

435
00:19:28,515 --> 00:19:29,907
and they've got Holly

436
00:19:29,994 --> 00:19:31,344
and there's nothing
I can do to save her.

437
00:19:31,431 --> 00:19:33,084
Hey, whoa, whoa.

438
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,261
Don't worry.
I can help you.

439
00:19:36,566 --> 00:19:38,002
Okay?

440
00:19:38,089 --> 00:19:39,395
What are you doing?

441
00:19:39,482 --> 00:19:40,962
- Calling the police.
- No, no, no.

442
00:19:41,049 --> 00:19:42,311
They said,
any hint of the cops,

443
00:19:42,398 --> 00:19:43,704
and they'll kill her.
They told me.

444
00:19:44,879 --> 00:19:47,098
Okay.

445
00:19:47,186 --> 00:19:49,536
Then we have to do it
the other way.

446
00:19:49,623 --> 00:19:50,972
What's the other way?

447
00:19:54,541 --> 00:19:55,933
I rob the casino for you.

448
00:19:57,326 --> 00:19:59,937
[instrumental music]

449
00:20:04,072 --> 00:20:05,465
Here's what
they sent me.

450
00:20:10,252 --> 00:20:11,601
You have any idea
who sent it?

451
00:20:11,688 --> 00:20:13,429
No.

452
00:20:13,516 --> 00:20:15,866
But you know how it is.
I meet all kinds of people.

453
00:20:15,953 --> 00:20:17,999
There's some hard cases in
this town. It could be anyone.

454
00:20:18,086 --> 00:20:19,827
Why now?

455
00:20:19,914 --> 00:20:22,308
The first of the month is
when the vault is the fullest

456
00:20:22,395 --> 00:20:24,614
so whoever's doing this
knows how the casino works.

457
00:20:24,701 --> 00:20:27,487
Okay. Well, I'll take a look
around and see what can be done.

458
00:20:27,574 --> 00:20:28,923
Can't be done.

459
00:20:29,010 --> 00:20:30,577
Vince and Skiddy agree

460
00:20:30,664 --> 00:20:32,361
and they've done things
like this before.

461
00:20:32,448 --> 00:20:34,450
And they're doing this out of
the goodness of their heart?

462
00:20:34,537 --> 00:20:36,322
Of course not.

463
00:20:36,409 --> 00:20:39,107
They don't know anything about
the kidnapping or about Holly.

464
00:20:39,194 --> 00:20:42,197
- Nobody can know.
- What about Trish?

465
00:20:42,284 --> 00:20:44,852
She's involved, isn't she?

466
00:20:44,939 --> 00:20:46,636
How much does she know?

467
00:20:46,723 --> 00:20:48,290
Only what Vince
and Skiddy know, nothing more.

468
00:20:49,639 --> 00:20:51,250
Okay.

469
00:20:51,337 --> 00:20:54,688
Well, we'll meet tomorrow
to discuss it more. Um..

470
00:20:54,775 --> 00:20:57,168
and I think we should
introduce me to your team.

471
00:20:58,692 --> 00:20:59,867
[car door opens]

472
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:02,478
Hey, Jane..

473
00:21:03,914 --> 00:21:06,613
...uh, thanks.

474
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,744
Yeah. Sure.

475
00:21:13,315 --> 00:21:15,796
- Hey. Found something.
- What is it?

476
00:21:15,883 --> 00:21:17,058
Remember Hellion
told Jane and Lisbon

477
00:21:17,145 --> 00:21:18,277
he didn't
know D'Stefano?

478
00:21:18,364 --> 00:21:20,627
- Yeah.
- Take a look at this.

479
00:21:20,714 --> 00:21:22,716
"Master of the dark arts
Jack Hellion performs magic

480
00:21:22,803 --> 00:21:25,371
with the help of
casino employee Ryan D'Stefano."

481
00:21:27,547 --> 00:21:29,418
- You told Lisbon yet?
- No. Just found it.

482
00:21:30,811 --> 00:21:32,769
What's with the flowers?

483
00:21:32,856 --> 00:21:36,120
- They're for Summer.
- Summer? Your CI?

484
00:21:36,207 --> 00:21:39,515
- Yeah.
- Oh. Okay.

485
00:21:39,602 --> 00:21:41,082
Goodnight.

486
00:21:41,169 --> 00:21:42,344
Hey. Nice work on Hellion.

487
00:21:42,431 --> 00:21:44,303
Yeah. Thanks. Goodnight.

488
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,089
Wow.

489
00:21:50,352 --> 00:21:51,484
[instrumental music]

490
00:21:55,052 --> 00:21:56,402
[knock on door]
That goes there..

491
00:21:56,489 --> 00:21:57,490
[Trish]
'Who is it?'

492
00:21:57,577 --> 00:21:59,840
[Vincent]
'It's us.'

493
00:21:59,927 --> 00:22:03,409
- 'Hey, boys.'
- What's this about, Hellion?

494
00:22:03,496 --> 00:22:05,672
You're late. Sit down.
We got a lot of work to do.

495
00:22:07,413 --> 00:22:08,936
what's he doing here?

496
00:22:09,023 --> 00:22:10,894
Jane's coming in
on the job with us.

497
00:22:10,981 --> 00:22:14,420
- 'Oh, yeah?'
- I don't know about that.

498
00:22:14,507 --> 00:22:15,943
How do we know
we can trust this guy?

499
00:22:16,030 --> 00:22:18,598
It's okay. You can trust him.
He's one of us.

500
00:22:18,685 --> 00:22:20,948
Says you. I'm not
doing this with him.

501
00:22:21,035 --> 00:22:24,778
Well, fine. Walk away
from a million bucks.

502
00:22:24,865 --> 00:22:25,996
Tell you the truth,
I didn't think

503
00:22:26,083 --> 00:22:27,607
you really had
the chops for it anyway.

504
00:22:27,694 --> 00:22:28,825
[scoffs]

505
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,568
[instrumental music]

506
00:22:41,098 --> 00:22:42,491
Show us your plan.

507
00:22:42,578 --> 00:22:44,711
Doesn't mean
that we agreed, though.

508
00:22:48,323 --> 00:22:51,631
Lounge, casino floor, vault

509
00:22:51,718 --> 00:22:53,372
'loading dock. Right?'

510
00:22:53,459 --> 00:22:55,809
First order of business,
the lock to the vault.

511
00:22:55,896 --> 00:22:57,376
Okay, it's a
high-security lock

512
00:22:57,463 --> 00:22:59,378
using a combination
of side wards and pins.

513
00:22:59,465 --> 00:23:00,857
I can get into it

514
00:23:00,944 --> 00:23:02,424
but it's gonna take
more time than we got.

515
00:23:02,511 --> 00:23:05,209
Security comes by
every five minutes.

516
00:23:05,296 --> 00:23:06,907
Then we're gonna need a key.

517
00:23:06,994 --> 00:23:08,474
[Skiddy]
Holmes the security chief

518
00:23:08,561 --> 00:23:10,563
carries it on him
at all times.

519
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,042
[Patrick]
I'll take care of that.

520
00:23:12,129 --> 00:23:14,349
The vault, you cased it
yesterday, right?

521
00:23:14,436 --> 00:23:17,526
Yeah. The door in the main room
of the casino

522
00:23:17,613 --> 00:23:19,485
marked authorized
personnel only

523
00:23:19,572 --> 00:23:21,487
accesses both
the backstage area

524
00:23:21,574 --> 00:23:23,532
and a hallway
that leads to the vault.

525
00:23:23,619 --> 00:23:26,535
There's a heavy steel gate,
then the door to the vault.

526
00:23:26,622 --> 00:23:28,885
There's a small window
set into it.

527
00:23:28,972 --> 00:23:31,671
Inside the vault is a bare room with the safe set in the wall.

528
00:23:31,758 --> 00:23:33,847
There's no place
to hide in there.

529
00:23:33,934 --> 00:23:35,239
There's cameras
outside the vault

530
00:23:35,326 --> 00:23:36,980
but we can
put them on a loop.

531
00:23:37,067 --> 00:23:38,895
Nobody'll know the difference. They're not the problem.

532
00:23:38,982 --> 00:23:40,549
The problem
is that the guards

533
00:23:40,636 --> 00:23:43,117
come and check the vault
every five to six minutes.

534
00:23:43,204 --> 00:23:45,336
The safe isn't complex,
but it's still gonna take me

535
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:47,469
more than six minutes
to crack it.

536
00:23:47,556 --> 00:23:49,689
Okay, so we need to get into
the vault without being seen

537
00:23:49,776 --> 00:23:51,560
we need to return
the key to Holmes

538
00:23:51,647 --> 00:23:54,520
before he realizes it's gone,
then we need to open the safe

539
00:23:54,607 --> 00:23:56,826
without being seen,
take the money, and get away.

540
00:23:58,045 --> 00:23:59,525
Yeah, that's all.

541
00:23:59,612 --> 00:24:01,570
Yeah. Well, if I can
figure out a way to do it

542
00:24:01,657 --> 00:24:03,224
you gotta go along
with what I say.

543
00:24:03,311 --> 00:24:05,313
No questions.
No arguments. Yes?

544
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:08,621
Yes, absolutely.

545
00:24:08,708 --> 00:24:10,405
You better be on the level.

546
00:24:11,928 --> 00:24:14,104
Or else we got a problem.

547
00:24:14,191 --> 00:24:17,891
Only problem I can foresee
is getting you ready in time.

548
00:24:17,978 --> 00:24:19,458
When are we pulling the job?

549
00:24:19,545 --> 00:24:20,676
Tonight.

550
00:24:22,199 --> 00:24:24,419
- Yeah.
- Let's get to work.

551
00:24:26,552 --> 00:24:28,423
Jane? We need to talk to you.

552
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:31,121
Well, that sounds ominous.
I need to talk to you as well.

553
00:24:31,208 --> 00:24:33,167
Your friend Jack Hellion
looks good for this.

554
00:24:33,254 --> 00:24:34,560
[chuckles]
You think?

555
00:24:34,647 --> 00:24:36,431
He knew our victim D'Stefano.

556
00:24:36,518 --> 00:24:38,041
And he was dating
Holly Danvers.

557
00:24:38,128 --> 00:24:39,608
We think they were
in it together.

558
00:24:39,695 --> 00:24:40,783
In what?

559
00:24:40,870 --> 00:24:42,568
The murder of Ryan D'Stefano.

560
00:24:42,655 --> 00:24:45,353
Oh.Yes. Uh..

561
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:47,224
Well, it's a theory.

562
00:24:48,443 --> 00:24:50,097
And you think it's wrong.

563
00:24:50,184 --> 00:24:52,665
Well, I know it's wrong.
I mean, it's way off the mark.

564
00:24:52,752 --> 00:24:54,275
I'm, I'm sorry.

565
00:24:54,362 --> 00:24:56,059
And you know the right story,
of course.

566
00:24:56,146 --> 00:24:58,758
Yes, I do, and I know how
to close this case neatly.

567
00:25:00,281 --> 00:25:02,065
So? Do tell.

568
00:25:02,152 --> 00:25:04,807
I shall, but we're in
a very tricky situation here.

569
00:25:04,894 --> 00:25:06,156
There is a life at stake

570
00:25:06,243 --> 00:25:07,984
and you're gonna
have to bear with me

571
00:25:08,071 --> 00:25:09,856
because what I'm about to say
might sound a little crazy

572
00:25:09,943 --> 00:25:11,771
'but..'

573
00:25:11,858 --> 00:25:13,729
Trust me.
It is the only way.

574
00:25:13,816 --> 00:25:15,296
He said, crazy idea.

575
00:25:15,383 --> 00:25:16,950
- He said, trust me.
- Always a bad sign.

576
00:25:17,037 --> 00:25:18,386
Well, listen,
I'm just a consultant here.

577
00:25:18,473 --> 00:25:19,866
We don't have to
do this all together.

578
00:25:19,953 --> 00:25:22,912
I mean, I can manage
on my own somehow.

579
00:25:22,999 --> 00:25:24,087
Wait.

580
00:25:29,179 --> 00:25:30,703
I will bear with you.

581
00:25:34,097 --> 00:25:35,272
Talk.

582
00:25:38,841 --> 00:25:39,973
[crickets chirping]

583
00:25:53,290 --> 00:25:55,336
[phone beeps]
Uh, it's the kidnappers.

584
00:25:55,423 --> 00:25:56,772
They've given us a location

585
00:25:56,859 --> 00:25:58,382
to drop the money
after the job is done.

586
00:25:58,469 --> 00:25:59,732
Well, tell 'em
we're not doing anything

587
00:25:59,819 --> 00:26:01,298
until we know
that Holly's alive.

588
00:26:01,385 --> 00:26:02,430
[whispers]
Okay.

589
00:26:05,955 --> 00:26:07,827
Oh. They're
sending something.

590
00:26:07,914 --> 00:26:09,698
[gasps]
Oh, my God.

591
00:26:15,791 --> 00:26:19,708
Okay, keep it together, Jack.
We got a job to do here.

592
00:26:19,795 --> 00:26:23,059
You okay?
Text them back.

593
00:26:23,146 --> 00:26:24,887
Tell 'em we'll take the money
to the drop site

594
00:26:24,974 --> 00:26:26,410
just like they said.

595
00:26:26,497 --> 00:26:27,629
[breathing heavily]

596
00:26:30,632 --> 00:26:31,720
Okay?

597
00:26:31,807 --> 00:26:33,330
Okay.

598
00:26:33,417 --> 00:26:34,854
Let's go.

599
00:26:36,595 --> 00:26:38,205
[knock on door]

600
00:26:38,292 --> 00:26:41,338
Hey. Hey, where have you two
been? We go on in four minutes.

601
00:26:41,425 --> 00:26:42,992
We ready?

602
00:26:43,079 --> 00:26:45,212
Uh, there is one small thing.
Uh, those police

603
00:26:45,299 --> 00:26:47,040
that are investigating
D'Stefano's murder

604
00:26:47,127 --> 00:26:48,824
they're here again.

605
00:26:48,911 --> 00:26:51,566
I just wanted you to know so you
don't freak out if you see them.

606
00:26:51,653 --> 00:26:53,002
Oh, crap.

607
00:26:53,089 --> 00:26:54,569
- We gotta call it off.
- No, no. No, we don't.

608
00:26:54,656 --> 00:26:56,571
Everything goes ahead
as planned.

609
00:26:56,658 --> 00:26:58,268
They're working a homicide.

610
00:26:58,355 --> 00:27:00,053
They're not even gonna be
thinking about a robbery.

611
00:27:00,140 --> 00:27:03,230
We do it right
under their noses. Okay?

612
00:27:03,317 --> 00:27:04,971
Okay.

613
00:27:05,058 --> 00:27:07,147
- Let's do this.
- Curtain's up.

614
00:27:13,936 --> 00:27:15,895
[instrumental music]

615
00:27:17,853 --> 00:27:20,160
[applause]

616
00:27:28,864 --> 00:27:31,388
Welcome, ladies and gentlemen.

617
00:27:31,475 --> 00:27:35,784
Tonight I will
delight and amaze you.

618
00:27:35,871 --> 00:27:38,918
[Jack]
'You will see things that will
make you doubt your eyes.'

619
00:27:41,355 --> 00:27:43,487
- You all set?
- Set.

620
00:27:43,574 --> 00:27:44,793
I can't believe
we're doing this.

621
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,577
I'mdoing this.

622
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,710
Well, yeah, but legally,
we're accomplices, so I mean--

623
00:27:48,797 --> 00:27:50,407
Could you shut up?

624
00:27:51,582 --> 00:27:52,714
[applause]

625
00:27:53,672 --> 00:27:55,151
[indistinct chatter]

626
00:27:55,238 --> 00:27:57,545
Hello, Grace. What luck
running into you here.

627
00:27:57,632 --> 00:27:59,068
Hi, Jane. Am I late?

628
00:27:59,155 --> 00:28:01,592
Not at all. Follow me.

629
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:04,639
My next demonstration
is something I learned

630
00:28:04,726 --> 00:28:07,816
from a yogi mystic
in Dharamshala.

631
00:28:07,903 --> 00:28:11,515
'How to see by using
your astral mind.'

632
00:28:11,602 --> 00:28:14,170
Not your physical senses.

633
00:28:14,257 --> 00:28:16,346
I will need a volunteer.

634
00:28:16,433 --> 00:28:17,565
[crowd murmuring]

635
00:28:19,567 --> 00:28:21,438
You, sir.

636
00:28:21,525 --> 00:28:22,918
[chuckles]
No.

637
00:28:23,005 --> 00:28:24,050
Come on, folks.
Give him a hand.

638
00:28:24,137 --> 00:28:27,401
- He's just shy.
- Go on.

639
00:28:27,488 --> 00:28:29,838
[instrumental music]

640
00:28:36,497 --> 00:28:39,674
I want you to
examine this hood.

641
00:28:39,761 --> 00:28:42,242
It's impossible to see
out of it. Is that not so?

642
00:28:42,329 --> 00:28:43,939
Okay. Uh..

643
00:28:45,506 --> 00:28:46,942
Yes, you can't see out of it.

644
00:28:48,683 --> 00:28:50,859
[Trish]
Thank you.
Please step over here.

645
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,997
[whispers]
Okay. It's coming up.

646
00:29:01,696 --> 00:29:03,480
Can you see?

647
00:29:03,567 --> 00:29:05,787
No. I'm completely blind.

648
00:29:05,874 --> 00:29:07,223
[Trish]
Great, now from our volunteer

649
00:29:07,310 --> 00:29:09,878
could I get an object?
Any object, please.

650
00:29:11,706 --> 00:29:13,839
[indistinct chatter]

651
00:29:13,926 --> 00:29:15,666
Can I have a spot
here, please?

652
00:29:17,233 --> 00:29:20,193
What is the first object
I am showing you?

653
00:29:22,325 --> 00:29:24,110
Is it a wallet?

654
00:29:24,197 --> 00:29:25,589
[crowd]
Ohh!

655
00:29:25,676 --> 00:29:27,809
[applause]

656
00:29:27,896 --> 00:29:30,072
You can go back to your seat.
Thank you.

657
00:29:31,944 --> 00:29:33,467
I will now come out
to the audience.

658
00:29:33,554 --> 00:29:35,730
'Anyone can give me
an object.'

659
00:29:38,515 --> 00:29:40,343
Okay. Hat and glasses.

660
00:29:58,274 --> 00:30:00,015
Dante Holmes.

661
00:30:00,102 --> 00:30:01,712
Like to introduce you
to Grace Van Pelt.

662
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,236
She's an agent at the CBI.

663
00:30:03,323 --> 00:30:05,194
She'd like to ask you
a few questions.

664
00:30:05,281 --> 00:30:07,588
I think you two are
gonna get along famously.

665
00:30:08,937 --> 00:30:10,199
Hi.

666
00:30:12,027 --> 00:30:15,509
So, um...you're
the head of security, huh?

667
00:30:15,596 --> 00:30:17,990
[instrumental music]

668
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:34,136
Nobody saw you, did they?

669
00:30:34,223 --> 00:30:35,921
Nobody saw us.
You get the key?

670
00:30:36,008 --> 00:30:37,661
Like candy from a baby.
We clear?

671
00:30:37,748 --> 00:30:38,880
[beeps]

672
00:30:41,013 --> 00:30:42,318
Clear.

673
00:30:48,542 --> 00:30:50,936
[dramatic music]

674
00:30:53,895 --> 00:30:55,027
Okay.

675
00:31:00,206 --> 00:31:01,990
All set.

676
00:31:02,077 --> 00:31:04,514
You have roughly
five and a half minutes.

677
00:31:09,606 --> 00:31:11,870
[Patrick]
'Good, good, good.'

678
00:31:22,228 --> 00:31:24,360
Okay, gentlemen, I have to
get this key back to Holmes

679
00:31:24,447 --> 00:31:26,362
before he realizes it's gone.

680
00:31:26,449 --> 00:31:27,624
Wait.

681
00:31:30,497 --> 00:31:31,977
My hands.

682
00:31:32,064 --> 00:31:33,282
What?

683
00:31:34,588 --> 00:31:36,111
I don't think
I can do this.

684
00:31:36,198 --> 00:31:38,809
I'm not cut out
to be a criminal.

685
00:31:39,898 --> 00:31:42,291
Alright.

686
00:31:42,378 --> 00:31:45,599
You're gonna have to get this
key back into Holmes' pocket.

687
00:31:45,686 --> 00:31:48,167
I'll stay here and help.
Right side jacket pocket.

688
00:31:48,254 --> 00:31:50,821
Remember,
right side jacket pocket.

689
00:31:50,909 --> 00:31:52,258
[whispers]
Okay.

690
00:31:56,827 --> 00:31:58,525
Okay, Jack.
Hey, look at this coin.

691
00:31:58,612 --> 00:32:00,962
Look at how bright that is.

692
00:32:01,049 --> 00:32:04,009
Look at the way
the light hits it. Eh?

693
00:32:09,188 --> 00:32:11,581
As you breathe

694
00:32:11,668 --> 00:32:14,715
you will feel your body
slowly relax.

695
00:32:14,802 --> 00:32:17,674
I think you will be able
to tell what I have now.

696
00:32:17,761 --> 00:32:19,894
Is it a pair of glasses?

697
00:32:19,981 --> 00:32:21,069
[applause]

698
00:32:21,156 --> 00:32:22,288
See you soon, I hope.

699
00:32:22,375 --> 00:32:24,290
Yeah, good luck.

700
00:32:24,377 --> 00:32:25,987
Do you have an object,
you'd like to share?

701
00:32:27,467 --> 00:32:29,512
When I click my fingers,
Jack

702
00:32:29,599 --> 00:32:32,428
you will feel
calm and relaxed.

703
00:32:33,821 --> 00:32:35,692
It'll be easy
to open the safe.

704
00:32:37,129 --> 00:32:40,088
When I click my fingers,
Jack

705
00:32:40,175 --> 00:32:44,701
you will open the safe with
great ease...and quickness.

706
00:32:44,788 --> 00:32:45,964
[fingers snapping]

707
00:32:48,705 --> 00:32:50,490
What do you say
we open the safe?

708
00:32:50,577 --> 00:32:52,753
Okay, here we go.

709
00:32:53,884 --> 00:32:55,016
[clicking]

710
00:32:56,409 --> 00:32:57,845
Grace, have you seen Jane?

711
00:32:57,932 --> 00:33:00,413
Um, he was here
a second ago.

712
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:02,197
- Oh.
- Careful, son.

713
00:33:02,284 --> 00:33:05,635
Excuse me, sir.
Um, which way to the bathroom?

714
00:33:05,722 --> 00:33:07,115
Right over there.

715
00:33:14,775 --> 00:33:18,083
Excuse me, agents.
I've gotta get back to work.

716
00:33:20,650 --> 00:33:23,566
[dramatic music]

717
00:33:28,615 --> 00:33:29,790
[keys jangling]

718
00:34:16,837 --> 00:34:18,012
[clacking]

719
00:34:22,625 --> 00:34:23,800
[clacking]

720
00:34:36,683 --> 00:34:37,814
[knock on door]

721
00:34:42,689 --> 00:34:44,169
You guys ready?

722
00:34:44,256 --> 00:34:47,085
Let's go. You need
to get back to the stage.

723
00:34:51,828 --> 00:34:53,178
Okay. I got the rest of this.

724
00:34:53,265 --> 00:34:55,571
Time to bring the van
round to the loading dock.

725
00:34:55,658 --> 00:34:56,833
Okay.

726
00:35:02,883 --> 00:35:05,407
[applause]
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

727
00:35:05,494 --> 00:35:09,150
And for our last demonstration
may I have another object?

728
00:35:10,760 --> 00:35:14,938
I think you will be able
to tell what I have now.

729
00:35:15,025 --> 00:35:17,854
You are holding...a set
of car keys.

730
00:35:18,899 --> 00:35:20,379
[applause]

731
00:35:23,164 --> 00:35:26,080
[instrumental music]

732
00:35:31,041 --> 00:35:32,173
[whooshing]

733
00:35:41,051 --> 00:35:43,967
[applause]

734
00:35:51,105 --> 00:35:54,021
[dramatic music]

735
00:36:18,350 --> 00:36:19,916
[grunting]

736
00:36:20,003 --> 00:36:21,309
Got it.

737
00:36:22,832 --> 00:36:23,964
[door closes]

738
00:36:26,706 --> 00:36:29,622
Okay. Me and Vinnie will follow
right behind you in the car.

739
00:36:29,709 --> 00:36:31,189
- You have the keys?
- 'Yep.'

740
00:36:31,276 --> 00:36:32,625
Alright, we get separated

741
00:36:32,712 --> 00:36:34,148
We meet at the truck stop
at I-90, okay?

742
00:36:34,235 --> 00:36:35,497
Oh, don't worry.
We won't get separated.

743
00:36:35,584 --> 00:36:37,847
- Okay.
- Well done, men.

744
00:36:37,934 --> 00:36:39,327
We did it. Congratulations.

745
00:36:39,414 --> 00:36:42,330
- Okay.
- Nicely done.

746
00:36:42,417 --> 00:36:44,114
Hey. Don't stick around.

747
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:48,031
CBI's gonna be crawling
all over the place very soon.

748
00:36:48,118 --> 00:36:49,859
Why'd he have to hug me, man?
I hate that.

749
00:36:49,946 --> 00:36:52,340
Who cares, bro?
We're rich.

750
00:36:55,865 --> 00:36:57,650
Open the car. Let's go.

751
00:36:57,737 --> 00:36:59,347
He took the keys.

752
00:37:00,392 --> 00:37:02,568
Bastard took the keys!

753
00:37:02,655 --> 00:37:04,657
That's not the worst of it.

754
00:37:04,744 --> 00:37:07,355
Let me see your hands.
You're under arrest.

755
00:37:14,971 --> 00:37:16,408
[car approaching]

756
00:37:18,279 --> 00:37:20,020
Heads up.
Here they come.

757
00:37:34,730 --> 00:37:35,862
[Holly grunting]

758
00:37:37,298 --> 00:37:38,517
Holly?

759
00:37:38,604 --> 00:37:40,214
- Whoa.
- Stop right there, Jack.

760
00:37:40,301 --> 00:37:42,347
Trish?

761
00:37:42,434 --> 00:37:44,262
Turn around...slowly.

762
00:37:45,741 --> 00:37:47,613
Open the back of the truck.

763
00:37:47,700 --> 00:37:48,831
Trish, what are you doing?

764
00:37:48,918 --> 00:37:51,486
Open it.
Let me see the money.

765
00:37:56,491 --> 00:37:58,188
[Jack]
'The money's in the box.'

766
00:38:00,408 --> 00:38:02,454
Oh, God.
It's gonna be alright, holly.

767
00:38:02,541 --> 00:38:05,195
- 'It's gonna be alright.'
- Yeah, sure it is.

768
00:38:05,283 --> 00:38:08,198
Get over there. Line up. Move.

769
00:38:10,984 --> 00:38:12,986
Trish, you don't
have to do this.

770
00:38:13,073 --> 00:38:15,858
He's right, you know.
You don't have to kill us.

771
00:38:15,945 --> 00:38:19,601
You're right. I don't,
but it's cleaner this way.

772
00:38:19,688 --> 00:38:21,734
Everybody who can identify me
will be dead

773
00:38:21,821 --> 00:38:24,998
and I will be on my way
to Mexico with a boxful of cash.

774
00:38:25,085 --> 00:38:28,044
Drop the gun
and put your hands in the air!

775
00:38:28,958 --> 00:38:30,133
[dramatic music]

776
00:38:34,399 --> 00:38:36,662
Blammo.

777
00:38:36,749 --> 00:38:39,404
Ballistics checks out
for the gun, Trish.

778
00:38:39,491 --> 00:38:41,057
Tell us why you did it
and we'll ask the DA

779
00:38:41,144 --> 00:38:43,625
to take the death penalty
off the table.

780
00:38:43,712 --> 00:38:45,627
What do you mean,
why did I do it?

781
00:38:45,714 --> 00:38:48,500
For the money, of course.
I was robbing a casino.

782
00:38:49,936 --> 00:38:51,981
Okay.

783
00:38:52,068 --> 00:38:53,548
You think I was bitter
because Jack was seeing

784
00:38:53,635 --> 00:38:55,594
some cheap-ass waitress
instead of me?

785
00:38:57,726 --> 00:38:59,815
You're 100% wrong.
Couldn't care less.

786
00:39:01,121 --> 00:39:03,341
It was strictly
about the money.

787
00:39:03,428 --> 00:39:05,386
Okay.

788
00:39:05,473 --> 00:39:07,910
It was D'Stefano that
gave me the idea at first

789
00:39:07,997 --> 00:39:11,349
always yammering on about
getting even with Holmes.

790
00:39:11,436 --> 00:39:13,176
And it was D'Stefano
who grabbed Holly?

791
00:39:13,263 --> 00:39:16,745
- Yes.
- Why did he kill the roommate?

792
00:39:16,832 --> 00:39:19,574
She was in the trailer,
she saw him.

793
00:39:19,661 --> 00:39:21,141
Bad luck for her.

794
00:39:26,059 --> 00:39:29,105
[Grace]
Once he brought you
Holly, you got rid of him.

795
00:39:29,192 --> 00:39:31,281
[Trish]
I couldn't trust him.

796
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:32,544
He killed that poor,
innocent girl

797
00:39:32,631 --> 00:39:34,372
without a shred of remorse.

798
00:39:39,289 --> 00:39:42,162
Even laughed about it.
No moral compass.

799
00:39:44,338 --> 00:39:46,993
You were about to kill
three innocent people yourself

800
00:39:47,080 --> 00:39:48,560
just a while ago.

801
00:39:48,647 --> 00:39:50,779
And I would have felt
terrible about it.

802
00:39:50,866 --> 00:39:52,607
There's a difference.

803
00:39:54,957 --> 00:39:56,785
You're nuts, lady.

804
00:39:57,917 --> 00:39:59,484
Sign here.

805
00:40:01,268 --> 00:40:05,141
We can never thank you enough.
I owe you big time.

806
00:40:05,228 --> 00:40:08,101
True. Big time.
Plus 50 bucks.

807
00:40:08,188 --> 00:40:10,059
You said
you'd let that slide.

808
00:40:10,146 --> 00:40:11,844
Ah, so you doadmit
that you owe me.

809
00:40:11,931 --> 00:40:15,108
No. Wait, when did I first
incur this debt, anyhow?

810
00:40:15,195 --> 00:40:17,893
You were opening for me in
Kansas City. I think it was '93.

811
00:40:17,980 --> 00:40:19,242
There was a girl,
not as attra--

812
00:40:19,329 --> 00:40:21,897
Opening for you? Please.
Never happened.

813
00:40:21,984 --> 00:40:23,421
What were the drugs
that you got busted for?

814
00:40:23,508 --> 00:40:24,987
You want to get
a cup of coffee?

815
00:40:25,074 --> 00:40:27,076
Because I have a feeling
this could go on for a while.

816
00:40:27,163 --> 00:40:29,818
'Cause whatever they are,
I'm afraid they've undermined

817
00:40:29,905 --> 00:40:31,690
the foundation
of your memory palace.

818
00:40:31,777 --> 00:40:33,996
I'm sorry. I've never seen
Jack like this before.

819
00:40:34,083 --> 00:40:36,782
No need to apologize.
Jane has that effect on people.

820
00:40:42,788 --> 00:40:45,355
[theme music]

